Fixed the `loadModel()` cache bug, added vitest tests, and updated the footer text.
### Changes
- **`web/src/data.js`**: Changed `modelCache.current` initial value from `null` to `undefined` so the guard `!== undefined` correctly allows the first fetch to proceed (previously `null !== undefined` was true, so it always returned `null` without fetching).
- **`web/src/data.test.js`**: Created new test file with 3 vitest tests: (1) fetches and returns parsed model on success, (2) returns `null` when fetch fails, (3) caches result so subsequent calls skip fetching. Uses dynamic imports with query params for fresh module state per test.
- **`web/src/App.jsx`**: Updated footer from "Built with PyCharm, WebStorm and Junie" to "Built with Junie, JetBrains' coding agent".
